    "recommendations": "Reducing the concentration of brush and vegetation in the immediate area surrounding the structure would improve defensible space and may reduce direct fuel exposure to the building. Where brush and scattered shrubs are present adjacent to the structure, creating greater horizontal separation between those fuel sources and the building could reduce fuel continuity near the improvement. Managing the mixed vegetation and tree clusters on the property to increase spacing between individual plants and between vegetation and the structure may further reduce opportunities for fire to travel toward the structure. Maintaining the access route by keeping overhanging and encroaching vegetation trimmed back along the driveway would support firefighter access and improve visibility for both ingress and egress during an emergency response. Ongoing vegetation management within the immediate structure perimeter, particularly where heavy brush is present, would support suppression operations and contribute to long-term wildfire resilience for the property."
